      "id": 1794641623794.7415,
      "question": "If it takes 5 minutes for one towel to dry, how long will it take seven towels to dry if they are spread on a rope?",
      "options": [
        "35 minutes",
        "5 minutes",
        "12 minutes",
        "70 minutes"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 1,
      "explanation": "Drying time depends on environmental conditions (like sun and wind) and exposure, not on the total number of items, as long as they are spread out.<br><br>Because the seven towels are hung on the rope simultaneously, they dry in parallel. Therefore, they will all take the same amount of time as a single towel.<br><br>• Option A (35 minutes) is a common trap; it comes from multiplying 5 minutes × 7 towels, which only applies if they were dried one after the other.<br>• Options C and D are random incorrect calculations.<br><br>The correct answer is <b>5 minutes</b>.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
